A||||2||GodSend||Easy way to get the top of the dash out?||||13||
Z||000000||GodSend||09-29-2001||11:15 AM||||I gave this a try last week.  I took out two bolts under the front speaker covers... two bols at the bottom near each door.<P>I know there are more bolts, but I cant figure out where (I also took the bolts off the passanger vent).<P>The upper dash seems stuck in the middle.  I cant figure out where any more bolts are.  Any help is greatly appreciated.<P>||||reg||13
Z||000001||David Bartlett||09-29-2001||11:42 AM||||I've had mine out twice now and from what I remember you goto take the metal support for the oil/volts gage off. Make sure all the bolts under there are gone. Then if memory serves me right its only held in with a plastic piece. Tilt and pull towards the seats.<BR>Don't foget to lower you stearing column down this makes it easier getting out. The 2nd time I didn't do this and it took longer then  the first time.<P>So basicaly its held in by the metal support stand and a clip.<P><BR>Good Luck.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Monkeyman||09-29-2001||01:18 PM||||Godsend--You didn't need to remove the screws at the vents.  You must remove the stereo/HVAC surround, the aux gauges (if you have them) and the metal piece that holds the dash to the plastic center console support.  The plastic center console support has a couple of little tabs that fit into the lower front of the center vent hole on the dash.  If you twist the dash so you're pulling the top towards you, You should be able to finagle it out of there.  Don't get frustrated.  It'll come out of there.||||reg||1
